"92a_appmixedstrip.mst — the Cocoa half of the Mixed Demo: the hand-built view.

 The provider `world/91d_appmixed.mst`'s spec names. This is DELIBERATELY the
 kind of code the framework exists to remove — alloc/initWithFrame:, colours,
 wiring — written out by hand to prove the escape hatch carries real AppKit:
 a dark strip, a label, and an NSButton built and wired IMPERATIVELY whose
 action dispatches the SAME #bump event the declarative button sends. The
 model cannot tell them apart, which is the point being made.

 THE VIEW IS REBUILT PER REALIZE (the provider block runs on every rebuild),
 and the realizer adopts it into the window's tree, so teardown removes it
 with everything else. The author holds no window and frees nothing — the
 bargain is unchanged even inside the hatch."

Object subclass: CocoaMixedStrip [
    <classVars: Delegates>

    CocoaMixedStrip class >> install [
        CocoaRealize provideForeign: #nativeStrip with: [ :node |
            CocoaMixedStrip buildStripFor: node ].
        ^self
    ]

    CocoaMixedStrip class >> buildStripFor: node <Object> ^ <Object> [
        | box label btn holder delegate |
        box := ((Cocoa classNamed: 'NSBox') onMain alloc) onMain
            initWithFrame: (Array with: 0.0 with: 0.0
                                  with: ((node at: #width) ifNil: [ 430 ]) asFloat
                                  with: ((node at: #height) ifNil: [ 64 ]) asFloat).
        box onMain setBoxType: 4.            "NSBoxCustom"
        box onMain setCornerRadius: 8.0.
        box onMain setFillColor:
            ((Cocoa classNamed: 'NSColor') onMain colorWithCalibratedRed: 0.13 green: 0.15 blue: 0.20 alpha: 1.0).
        label := ((Cocoa classNamed: 'NSTextField') onMain alloc) onMain
            initWithFrame: (Array with: 14.0 with: 20.0 with: 240.0 with: 18.0).
        label onMain setEditable: false. label onMain setBordered: false.
        label onMain setDrawsBackground: false. label onMain setSelectable: false.
        label onMain setStringValue: 'I am a hand-built NSView'.
        label onMain setTextColor: ((Cocoa classNamed: 'NSColor') onMain whiteColor).
        box onMain addSubview: label.
        btn := ((Cocoa classNamed: 'NSButton') onMain alloc) onMain
            initWithFrame: (Array with: 280.0 with: 14.0 with: 130.0 with: 28.0).
        btn onMain setTitle: 'Bump (native)'.
        btn onMain setBezelStyle: 1.
        "Wired BY HAND — and into the app's own event loop: the same #bump
         the declarative button sends, through the same dispatch."
        holder := CocoaToolbarAction on: [
            (AppToolWindow named: #mixed) ifNotNil: [ :w | w dispatch: #bump value: nil ] ].
        delegate := MacvmDelegate actionTargetOn: holder.
        btn onMain setTarget: delegate.
        btn onMain setAction: 'macvmAction:'.
        "RETAIN THE DELEGATE, and this line was earned the honest way: without
         it the strip WORKED, then went silently dead a GC later. An
         NSControl's target is weak; the holder survives in the world-side
         ticket registry but the ObjcRef delegate does not, and once it was
         collected every click went nowhere with nothing raised anywhere.
         The framework's own wire:to: retains for exactly this reason — a
         provider that hand-wires must hand-retain. In the cookbook's traps."
        Delegates isNil ifTrue: [ Delegates := OrderedCollection new ].
        Delegates add: delegate.
        box onMain addSubview: btn.
        ^box
    ]
]
